This is a diagnosis (break-and-fix) lesson, so it opts out of the structural
parity gate (src/verify-parity.py).

Unlike a normal scaffold, the before/ code is not full of TODOs — it runs, but
carries a planted bug (a mismatched embedder) that the student must diagnose from
a failing eval and fix. The after/ side adds the regression test that would have
caught it, so before/ and after/ test files legitimately differ.

verify-lessons.sh still applies: before must lint + type-check clean and fail its
tests; after must be fully green.
